{
  "module": "modulo03-mcp-na-pratica/05-mcps-do-zero-z",
  "concepts": [
    "model-context-protocol",
    "symmetric-encryption",
    "schema-validation"
  ],
  "recorded": "Every case passed 50 runs against the original with Node.js 26.12.1, @modelcontextprotocol/sdk 1.27.1, and zod 3.25.76, run unchanged as node src/index.ts, the file npm start runs with type stripping. The server calls no model and needs no service. The ciphertexts decrypt_message receives were recorded from the original's encrypt_message on 2026-10-27, so a transcription that derives another key fails. The IV is random, so every encryption is checked by shape: 32 lowercase hex digits of IV that are not all zeros, a colon, and 32 hex digits for each block its UTF-8 bytes pad to, with the structured content equal to the text and a second encryption of the same message different from the first. A failed decryption is checked by the lesson's text up to Error details: followed by any message, since each library words it differently. Invalid arguments and unknown tools may come back as a tool result with isError or as a JSON-RPC error with code -32602. Tools and the prompt's arguments are compared in any order, capabilities by presence, and the protocol version not at all.",
  "prepare": { "setup": ["npm ci"] },
  "originals": ["node src/index.ts"],
